# Dialog Escape to close

Modal popups and dialogs must close when the user presses **Escape**.

## Pattern

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!open) return;
  const onKey = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
    if (e.key === "Escape" && !busy) onOpenChange(false);
  };
  window.addEventListener("keydown", onKey);
  return () => window.removeEventListener("keydown", onKey);
}, [open, busy, onOpenChange]);
```

## Rules

- Wire Escape on every new modal/`createPortal` dialog.
- Skip close while a blocking busy state is active (upload, send, save) when dismissing would be unsafe.
- Prefer matching existing dialogs (e.g. `assign-assets-to-staff-dialog.tsx`).
